    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d431">

                <pb facs="0564" n="484" sameAs="frus:frus1901/pg484"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Duke de Arcos.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-10-09"><hi rendition="#italic">October 9,
                        1901.</hi></date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 233.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your note of the 25th ultimo,
                    asking at the instance of the Spanish consul at New Orleans whether there is not
                    some means, pending the consideration of a new treaty, to avoid the exemption
                    from punishment of deserters from Spanish vessels in the United States, with
                    particular reference to the recent desertion of some of the crew of the
                    Barcelona steamship <hi rendition="#italic">Puerto Rico</hi>, I have the honor
                    to inform you that the Secretary of the Treasury, to whom the matter was
                    referred, reports that his Department is not aware of any law or regulation
                    providing for the punishment of deserters under the circumstances such as you
                    describe. It may be stated further that in the act approved December 2, 1898,
                    Congress formally repealed the laws then existing which authorized the arrest of
                    deserters from vessels of the United States in ports in this country.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
